  "query_preview": "..The strong Pacific low that brought strong southwest \nwinds to the region has shifted to the east across the northern \nRockies. As the low lifts a bit more to the north, the flow will \nturn more westerly. However, the gradient will remain sufficiently \ntight that we will continue to see breezy conditions through the end \nof the week. Expect daytime southwest to west winds around 20-20 mph \nwith gusts to 30 mph today and Friday. RH values are between 10-20% \nthis afternoon and with the strongest winds across the eastern \nLittle Colorado River Valley, there will be near-critical fire \nweather concerns there, mainly right along the NM border. \nTemperatures will be near to slightly below average today, returning \nto near to slightly above average on Friday. A weak shortwave will \npass through on Friday but other than an increase in cloud cover, it \nwill be uneventful. \n\nThe weekend continues to look unsettled as several shortwaves move \nthrough the region. Moisture increases on Saturday with some slight \nchances for high-based showers arriving by Saturday afternoon with \nchances continuing through. As the waves move through the region \nSaturday night and Sunday. Models keep increasing the moisture with \neach subsequent run but confidence still remains low as to just how \nmuch we will see across the area. Therefore, you should expect \nincreasing cloudiness over the weekend with some chances for showers \nthrough Sunday and then again around midweek. Temperatures will \ncool, dropping 5-15 degrees below average by Sunday and then warming \nto near average again early next week. Expect breezy afternoons to \ncontinue over the weekend and through much of next week.",
